    narr:narration """This sample is a review-comment record from [Tina's review of the perspective](narr:Expr_20260929_1_ReviewCommentsTinaTeammember20260924_h1feabda3f4e2_1), where [each section quotes what was under review first, then gives the reviewer's own words](narr:Expr_20260929_1_ReviewCommentsTinaTeammember20260924_h1feabda3f4e2_2). The quoted perspective opens by asking [how the minimum soak duration between site cutovers is determined and validated](narr:Expr_20260929_1_ReviewCommentsTinaTeammember20260924_h1feabda3f4e2_3). The exchange then moves through [the concession that the correction is right but costs something, since one week has no slack](narr:Expr_20260929_1_ReviewCommentsTinaTeammember20260924_h1feabda3f4e2_4), [the reply preferring defensible-with-known-slack over conservatism for an imaginary reason](narr:Expr_20260929_1_ReviewCommentsTinaTeammember20260924_h1feabda3f4e2_5), and [the on-the-record caveat that the new number is tight, not safe](narr:Expr_20260929_1_ReviewCommentsTinaTeammember20260924_h1feabda3f4e2_6). It closes with [the formal for-the-record statement that the soak is one week and the eighth's two-week note is superseded](narr:Expr_20260929_1_ReviewCommentsTinaTeammember20260924_h1feabda3f4e2_7), backed by [the speaker's own retraction of the eighth's two-week hold](narr:Expr_20260929_1_ReviewCommentsTinaTeammember20260924_h1feabda3f4e2_8). Against that settlement, [Tina's comment that the soak should be two weeks because the batch jobs only run weekly](narr:Expr_20260929_1_ReviewCommentsTinaTeammember20260924_h1feabda3f4e2_10) stands as the open technical objection.""" ;
